ot diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -6.2% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Adobe (ADBE) screens at opportunity 73.0 with an expectations gap of 28.0. Reality 60.0 reflects +12.0% TTM revenue growth, +35.7% operating margin and +59.4% ROIC; pricing 32.0 reflects a depressed multiple and neutral price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Software & Agents (trend 71.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["EV/Sales 3.6x (5.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 13x (5.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 11.3%","PEG 1.1","12m return -34%, -34% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (60.0) is running ahead of what is priced (32.0): an expectations gap of +28 pts.","Its main theme (AI Software & Agents) has trend 71.0 vs pricing 52.0: the theme itself is under-owned."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-09-22)","AI Software & Agents: evidence that 'Trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is easing via Platforms owning the system of record and the data","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 7% (currently 12.0%)","ROIC falls below 45% (currently 59.4%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 35.7%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +73)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.0703,"current":0.1203},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.4452,"current":0.5935},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":-0.005463174840933449},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":73.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.599999999999994},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":-8.7},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Software & Agents theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-software-agents","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":71.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-software-agents","theme":"AI Software & Agents","weight":0.4,"order":1,"effective":0.4}],"llm":{"thesis":"Adobe is priced as a melting ice cube while still behaving like a compounder: 12.0% TTM revenue growth (accelerating from 11.5%), 35.7% operating margins, 40.8% FCF margin and 59.4% ROIC, yet the stock trades at 12.9x earnings and 8.8x free cash flow \u2014 the 5th percentile of its own five-year range versus a 28.6x median P/E. The 11.3% FCF yield plus a 9.9% buyback yield (diluted shares -6.2% YoY) means shareholders are being paid a double-digit cash return simply for the business not shrinking. The gap between measured reality (60) and pricing (32) is 28 points, and the primary theme exposure \u2014 AI Software & Agents, trend 71 versus theme pricing 52 \u2014 is itself under-owned. The honest bear counterweight is that net income grew only 4.7% against 12% revenue, operating margin slipped 55bps, and SBC is 8.0% of revenue: the market is not mispricing the trailing numbers, it is discounting terminal value in a world where generative AI commoditizes content creation. This is a valuation-and-cash-return trade, not a growth-reacceleration trade; it works if revenue growth merely holds near double digits for four to six quarters.","fundamental_read":"Growth is modestly accelerating (+12.0% vs +11.5%) with best-in-class unit economics: 89.3% gross margin, 40.8% FCF margin, 1.45x FCF conversion, 59.4% ROIC and 148.9% incremental ROIC. The balance sheet is effectively unlevered (net debt/EBITDA 0.07x, interest coverage 35.7x), and $9.3bn of buybacks against a $93.7bn cap is retiring ~10% of the float annually \u2014 which is why EPS grew 11.9% while net income grew only 4.7%. The blemishes are real: operating margin fell 55bps YoY and SBC at 8.0% of revenue means a meaningful slice of that 11.3% FCF yield is recycled into offsetting dilution rather than accruing to holders.","technical_read":"The tape is in a downtrend: price 240.69 sits below the 20- (264.11), 50- (257.13) and 200-day (263.74) averages, 8.7% under the 200dma and 33.5% off the 52-week high, with RSI 39 and negative MACD histogram. The +22.4% three-month return followed by -12.9% over one month shows a failed rally that rolled over, so momentum offers no confirmation yet. A reclaim of the 257\u2013264 moving-average cluster on volume would be the first technical evidence that the de-rating is exhausted; until then buyers are catching a knife on valuation alone.","market_expectation":"At 3.6x EV/Sales and 9.4x EV/EBITDA versus 7.6x and 19.6x historical medians, the market is pricing structural impairment \u2014 that AI collapses the price of creative output, erodes seat growth and pricing power, and that today's 12% growth decays toward low single digits with permanent margin compression. A 1.1 PEG and -34% twelve-month return say consensus has moved from 'quality compounder' to 'value trap under disruption.' Essentially nothing is priced for Adobe monetizing AI successfully; the multiple assumes Firefly and agentic workflows are a defensive cost, not a revenue line.","what_market_misses":["The expectations gap is 28 points: reality (60) is running materially ahead of pricing (32), and revenue is accelerating, not decelerating \u2014 the disruption narrative has not yet shown up in the reported numbers.","Mechanical shareholder return: at 8.8x FCF with ~10% of the float retired annually, flat revenue and flat margins still deliver roughly a low-teens IRR without any multiple re-rating.","The AI Software & Agents theme carries trend 71 against theme pricing 52 \u2014 the theme is under-owned, and Adobe is the rare AI-exposed name trading at 12.9x rather than a premium.","Proprietary data plus system-of-record ownership (creative files, document workflows, marketing data) is the exact moat that generic models lack; if trust and workflow integration are the binding constraint on AI adoption, incumbents with the data are the beneficiaries, not the victims.","Technology sector rotation score is +73, the only strongly positive sector in the entire rotation table, yet ADBE trades below its 200dma \u2014 a rare divergence between sector flow and single-name price."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-09-22 filing): any print holding double-digit revenue growth with stabilized operating margin directly contradicts the terminal-decline thesis.","Disclosure of AI-attributable ARR or seat/pricing uplift that converts Firefly from a cost narrative into a revenue narrative.","Continued buyback at depressed prices \u2014 at 8.8x FCF, each quarter of repurchase is unusually accretive and compounds EPS growth above revenue growth.","Continued capital rotation into Technology (+73) eventually pulling the laggards in the sector.","Operating margin returning to YoY expansion, reversing the -55bps trend that anchors the bear case."],"risks":["Net income growth of 4.7% versus revenue growth of 12.0% shows genuine profit-quality erosion beneath the headline; if this widens, the 'cheap' multiple is cheap for a reason.","SBC at 8.0% of revenue means reported FCF overstates economic owner earnings; the true FCF yield to holders is lower than 11.3%.","Generative AI could compress seat counts and per-seat pricing faster than Adobe can monetize AI features \u2014 a true value trap outcome where multiple and estimates fall together.","Technicals are actively negative: below all major moving averages, MACD negative, -33.5% from the high; cheap stocks in downtrends frequently get cheaper.","Estimate-revision and management-guidance feeds are not connected (coverage 0.75), so the thesis rests on trailing fundamentals and valuation without forward confirmation.","Regime probabilities are near-uniform (Goldilocks 26.3, Reflation 25.1, Stagflation 23.7, Contraction 24.9) \u2014 there is no macro tailwind, and macro fit for Technology is only 53/100."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 7% (currently 12.0%).","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY (currently 35.7%, -55bps).","Net income growth stays below half of revenue growth for two more quarters, confirming structural profit erosion rather than a one-off.","Buyback pace decelerates materially from the ~$9.3bn annualized run-rate, removing the mechanical EPS support.","ROIC falls below 45% (currently 59.4%).","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +73).","Price closes more than 10% below the 200dma with negative relative strength, or fails twice at the 257\u2013264 moving-average cluster.","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Cloud and inference compute providers: Adobe's generative features are a variable-cost obligation \u2014 every Firefly render is someone else's revenue, which is part of why gross margin (89.3%) and operating margin are under pressure.","AI accelerator and inference-chip vendors selling into the creative/media inference workload as it scales from experiment to default.","Content provenance, watermarking and digital-rights infrastructure: if trust is the binding constraint on AI adoption in commercial creative work, whoever certifies authenticity monetizes it.","Data-labeling and licensed-content suppliers, since commercially safe training corpora are the scarce input for enterprise-indemnified generative output.","Competing distribution layers (design tools embedded in collaboration and marketing suites) that capture the low-end seats Adobe may cede \u2014 the direct source of the bear case, and the hedge against this long.","Systems integrators and marketing-services firms monetizing the workflow rewiring that agentic creative tools require inside large enterprises."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue grew 12.0%, accelerating from 11.5% in the prior quarter.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E is 12.9x and EV/EBITDA 9.4x, both at the 5th percentile of the five-year range versus medians of 28.6x and 19.6x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"FCF yield is 11.3% and buyback yield 9.9%, with diluted shares down 6.2% YoY.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin of 35.7% declined 55bps YoY and net income grew only 4.7%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price is below the 20-, 50- and 200-day moving averages with RSI 39 and negative MACD.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market expects generative AI to structurally impair Adobe's seat growth and pricing power, driving revenue growth toward low single digits.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Analysts broadly view the -34% twelve-month drawdown as disruption risk rather than a cyclical de-rating.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"At 8.8x FCF with ~10% annual share retirement, flat fundamentals still produce a low-teens IRR without multiple expansion.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"SBC at 8.0% of revenue means economic owner earnings are materially below reported FCF, so the true yield is lower than 11.3%.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Ownership of proprietary creative and document data plus the system of record is the durable moat generic models cannot replicate.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Adobe's rising generative-AI inference costs are a direct explanation for the 55bps margin erosion despite 89.3% gross margins.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Adobe will disclose AI-attributable revenue within the next few quarters, re-rating the stock toward its historical multiple.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.56}},"technical":{"score":0,"passes":0,"criteria":{"above_150_200":false,"150_above_200":false,"200_rising_1m":false,"50_above_150_200":false,"above_50":false,"25pct_above_52w_low":false,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":false,"rs_positive_6m":false},"ready":false,"stage":"basing_or_downtrend","close":240.69,"sma50":257.13,"sma150":246.55,"sma200":263.74,"sma150_prev4w":248.69,"sma150_declining":true,"pct_above_52w_low":24.4,"pct_from_52w_high":-33.5,"rs_6m":-15.4,"rsi14":39.2,"atr20":10.285,"atr_pct":4.27,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-08-28","filed":"2026-09-22","revenue":25970000000.0,"gross_profit":23179000000.0,"operating_income":9271000000.0,"net_income":7284000000.0,"ebitda":10037000000.0,"ocf":10806000000.0,"capex":214000000.0,"fcf":10592000000.0,"eps":17.91,"shares_diluted":406550000.0,"cash":5639000000.0,"debt":6363000000.0,"net_debt":724000000.0,"equity":11764000000.0,"total_assets":29981000000.0,"rnd":null,"sbc":2073000000.0,"buybacks":9295000000.0,"dividends":null,"gross_margin":0.8925298421255294,"operating_margin":0.3569888332691567,"net_margin":0.28047747400847134,"fcf_margin":0.4078552175587216,"fcf_conversion":1.4541460735859417,"revenue_growth":0.12031405029981457,"revenue_growth_prev":0.11490642006990837,"revenue_a